cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "SpectraQuant: Budget-Aware Joint Low-Rank and Low-Bit Training for Efficient Transformers"
abstract: >-
  Research software for studying whether low-rank preparation helps or hurts subsequent
  quantization of transformers, and whether an output-aware sensitivity proxy can allocate
  layer-wise ranks and bit widths that beat uniform compression at equal memory. Tier 0/1
  (synthetic and tiny-transformer) experiments run on CPU; Tier 2-5 are planned and require an
  external GPU.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Harrabi
    given-names: Oussema
    affiliation: "Independent research"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OussemaHarrabi/SpectraQuant"
url: "https://github.com/OussemaHarrabi/SpectraQuant"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0.dev0
keywords:
  - quantization
  - low-rank factorization
  - quantization-aware training
  - model compression
  - sensitivity analysis
  - efficient transformers
  - reproducibility
